{"parentUuid":"6cf49d17-9222-4089-a69c-9bcf14c423f8","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"94bdde78-3073-4c9c-ba60-6dad6ffce4f1","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"vast-shimmying-wadler","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_vrtx_0116PvRF1zL45vf1Zk9jUbeL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_017D277drufzAov1gXsofu2q","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/pandas-excel-analysis.md","content":"# Pandas and Excel Data Analysis Skill\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers reading and analyzing large Excel files using Python's pandas library, extracting specific data, and performing calculations on structured data.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install pandas openpyxl xlrd\n```\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### Reading Excel Files\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read Excel file with specific sheet\ndf = pd.read_excel('/path/to/file.xlsx', sheet_name='Sheet1')\n\n# Read multiple sheets\nxls_file = pd.ExcelFile('/path/to/file.xlsx')\nprint(xls_file.sheet_names)\n\n# Read specific columns\ndf = pd.read_excel('/path/to/file.xlsx', usecols=['col1', 'col2'])\n```\n\n### Basic Data Exploration\n```python\n# View structure\ndf.head()          # First 5 rows\ndf.shape           # Dimensions (rows, columns)\ndf.columns         # Column names\ndf.dtypes          # Data types\ndf.info()          # Summary information\n\n# Basic statistics\ndf.describe()      # Summary statistics\ndf['column'].unique()  # Unique values\n```\n\n### Filtering and Selection\n```python\n# Filter rows by condition\nfiltered = df[df['column'] > value]\n\n# Filter multiple conditions\nfiltered = df[(df['col1'] > 5) & (df['col2'] == 'value')]\n\n# Select specific rows by index\ndf.loc[index]\ndf.iloc[0:10]      # First 10 rows\n```\n\n### Data Processing\n```python\n# Apply functions to columns\ndf['new_col'] = df['col'].apply(lambda x: x * 2)\n\n# Group by operations\ngrouped = df.groupby('category')['value'].sum()\n\n# Comparison operations\ndf['winner'] = df['score1'] > df['score2']\n```\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\n### Large File Handling\n- Read specific sheets to avoid loading everything\n- Use `chunksize` parameter for very large files\n- Filter early to reduce memory usage\n\n### Calculation Workflows\n1. Load data\n2. Clean/validate data\n3. Calculate derived columns\n4. Group and aggregate\n5. Export results\n\n## Best Practices\n- Always check data types after reading\n- Use vectorized operations instead of loops\n- Memory-efficient filtering before processing\n- Validate assumptions about data structure\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":43969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":350,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbCQm3JcfSfrrpiPmvNP","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e1a59cb-22c8-4b4d-a7f8-83669dfe2d49","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:29:39.515Z"}
