nctions to columns\ndf['new_col'] = df['col'].apply(lambda x: x * 2)\n\n# Group by operations\ngrouped = df.groupby('category')['value'].sum()\n\n# Comparison operations\ndf['winner'] = df['score1'] > df['score2']\n```\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\n### Large File Handling\n- Read specific sheets to avoid loading everything\n- Use `chunksize` parameter for very large files\n- Filter early to reduce memory usage\n\n### Calculation Workflows\n1. Load data\n2. Clean/validate data\n3. Calculate derived columns\n4. Group and aggregate\n5. Export results\n\n## Best Practices\n- Always check data types after reading\n- Use vectorized operations instead of loops\n- Memory-efficient filtering before processing\n- Validate assumptions about data structure\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e1a59cb-22c8-4b4d-a7f8-83669dfe2d49"}
{"parentUuid":"ca1637fb-00d7-48c4-adb7-3df910387292","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"94bdde78-3073-4c9c-ba60-6dad6ffce4f1","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"vast-shimmying-wadler","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_vrtx_01CMEEkCdBxJVBFfkhWhVn6D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GeeNLeuz5R5GrWMwnXk6Sf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/game-matching-logic.md","content":"# Game Matching and Win Calculation Skill\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers logic for matching players in games and determining match winners based on game scores.\n\n## Problem Structure\n\n### Player Assignment\n- **Odd-numbered games** (1, 3, 5, ...): Played by Player 1\n- **Even-numbered games** (2, 4, 6, ...): Played by Player 2\n\n### Match Formation\nGames are paired off sequentially:\n- Match 1: Game 1 vs Game 2\n- Match 2: Game 3 vs Game 4\n- Match 3: Game 5 vs Game 6\n- Match n: Game (2n-1) vs Game (2n)\n\n### Win Determination\nFor each match:\n```\nIf score(odd_game) > score(even_game):\n    Player 1 wins match\nElse:\n    Player 2 wins match\n```\n\n## Implementation Logic\n\n### Extracting Game Scores\n```python\n# From loaded data, get game scores\n# Typically stored in columns like:\n# - Game_ID, Score, Player, or similar\n\n# Filter by odd/even game numbers\nplayer1_games = data[data['Game_ID'] % 2 == 1]  # Odd games\nplayer2_games = data[data['Game_ID'] % 2 == 0]  # Even games\n```\n\n### Pairing Games into Matches\n```python\n# For each pair of consecutive games\nmatches = []\nfor i in range(0, len(games), 2):\n    if i+1 < len(games):\n        match = {\n            'game1_id': games[i],\n            'game2_id': games[i+1],\n            'game1_score': games[i].score,\n            'game2_score': games[i+1].score,\n            'winner': 1 if games[i].score > games[i+1].score else 2\n        }\n        matches.append(match)\n```\n\n### Counting Wins\n```python\n# Count matches won by each player\nmatches_p1 = sum(1 for m in matches if m['winner'] == 1)\nmatches_p2 = sum(1 for m in matches if m['winner'] == 2)\ndifference = matches_p1 - matches_p2\n```\n\n## Edge Cases to Handle\n- Uneven number of games (last game unpaired)\n- Ties in game scores (need clarification on tie-breaking)\n- Data validation (ensure all games have scores)\n\n## Validation Checklist\n- [ ] Total games is even or handle odd case\n- [ ] All game IDs present\n- [ ] All games have valid scores\n- [ ] Match count = floor(total_games / 2)\n- [ ] Player 1 matches + Player 2 matches = Total matches\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":44319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":679,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":24}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbCRDNag6jpoXr8qmfdH","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e3e20a1-2b90-4a0f-ac10-51aee7992179","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:29:46.008Z"}
{"parentUuid":"4e3e20a1-2b90-4a0f-ac10-51aee7992179","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"94bdde78-3073-4c9c-ba60-6dad6ffce4f1","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"vast-shimmying-wadler","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01GeeNLeuz5R5GrWMwnXk6Sf","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/game-matching-logic.md"}]},"uuid":"3755a7a0-744c-4ab3-879c-c941c6d6c326","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:29:46.054Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/game-matching-logic.md","content":"# Game Matching and Win Calculation Skill\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers logic for matching players in games and determining match winners based on game scores.\n\n## Problem Structure\n\n### Player Assignment\n- **Odd-numbered games** (1, 3, 5, ...): Played by Player 1\n- **Even-numbered games** (2, 4, 6, ...): Played by Player 2\n\n### Match Formation\nGames are paired off sequentially:\n- Match 1: Game 1 vs Game 2\n- Match 2: Game 3 vs Game 4\n- Match 3: Game 5 vs Game 6\n- Match n: Game (2n-1) vs Game (2n)\n\n### Win Determination\nFor each match:\n```\nIf score(odd_game) > score(even_game):\n    Player 1 wins match\nElse:\n    Player 2 wins match\n```\n\n## Implementation Logic\n\n### Extracting Game Scores\n```python\n# From loaded data, get game scores\n# Typically stored in columns like:\n# - Game_ID, Score, Player, or similar\n\n# Filter by odd/even game numbers\nplayer1_games = data[data['Game_ID'] % 2 == 1]  # Odd games\nplayer2_games = data[data['Game_ID'] % 2 == 0]  # Even games\n```\n\n### Pairing Games into Matches\n```python\n# For each pair of consecutive games\nmatches = []\nfor i in range(0, len(games), 2):\n    if i+1 < len(games):\n        match = {\n            'game1_id': games[i],\n            'game2_id': games[i+1],\n            'game1_score': games[i].score,\n            'game2_score': games[i+1].score,\n            'winner': 1 if games[i].score > games[i+1].score else 2\n        }\n        matches.append(match)\n```\n\n### Counting Wins\n```python\n# Count matches won by each player\nmatches_p1 = sum(1 for m in matches if m['winner'] == 1)\nmatches_p2 = sum(1 for m in matches if m['winner'] == 2)\ndifference = matches_p1 - matches_p2\n```\n\n## Edge Cases to Handle\n- Uneven number of games (last game unpaired)\n- Ties in game scores (need clarification on tie-breaking)\n- Data validation (ensure all games have scores)\n\n## Validation Checklist\n- [ ] Total games is even or handle odd case\n- [ ] All game IDs present\n- [ ] All games have valid scores\n- [ ] Match count = floor(total_games / 2)\n- [ ] Player 1 matches + Player 2 matches = Total matches\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4e3e20a1-2b90-4a0f-ac10-51aee7992179"}
